I did not add either of the operations team's requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so there is no interface for writing a log file or for making an HTTP request to the metadata service. Adding either would need new grants, such as `http-client` for the fetch, which has to be done at the graph level.

The state key and the stored format are assumptions, because the spec doesn't name them. The node reads the key `urls` from the `subscriptions` store and treats the value as newline-separated URLs. If the key is missing, it returns an empty list and does not make up URLs, so `present(urls)` then depends on what the store holds.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(|l| l.trim())
                .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                .map(|l| l.to_string())
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

